	(footprint "cec-Connector_Screw:XFCN_TTR32100127-0600_Daughterboard_BoltPad_M3_PROVISIONAL"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c55b00ed-c6e5-4a51-a3c1-361856e871ad")
		(at 42.25 16.5)
		(descr "PROVISIONAL two-sided exposed-copper M3 bolt pad for a vertical daughterboard fastened to the threaded face of XFCN TTR32100127-0600. Primary current/heat interface is direct flat terminal-face to exposed F.Cu land; the B.Cu washer distributes preload and is not credited as a parallel conductor or thermal path. Do not insert grease, elastomer, thermal pad, or unspecified conforming material. Use a 3.4 mm normal-clearance plated hole. Place the hole center 4.5 mm above the daughterboard bottom-edge datum only as a drawing-envelope starting point, then correct screw-axis height, face flatness/finish, and washer/contact geometry from incoming-part measurement and coupon qualification before release. Add symmetric via stitching outside the measured contact area.")
		(tags "XFCN TTR32100127-0600 daughterboard bolt pad M3 clearance provisional sample verify")
